The chairperson shall administer the affairs and day-to-day business of the county and preside over the meetings of the board. The duties of the chairperson shall include, but shall not be limited to, the following:
(1) Calling meetings of the board as provided in Section 9 of this Act;
(2) Preparing a proposed agenda and presiding over meetings of the board;
(3) Representing the county government at ceremonial functions;
(4) Being empowered to submit motions that are made and seconded by district commissioners to the board for action;
(5) Appointing members and chairpersons to all committees of the board with the approval of the board; and
(6) Performing such other duties as shall be delegated to the chairperson by the board or as provided by law or ordinance.
The chairperson shall be authorized, in his or her sole discretion, to spend not more than $25,000.00 without approval of the board.
(2017 Ga. Laws (Act No. 165), § 10)

